            "Microcrystalline quartz (trigonal) in tightly packed fibres. No cleavage; conchoidal to uneven fracture. Hardness 6.5 to 7; specific gravity 2.55 to 2.64; waxy to vitreous lustre when polished; opaque to translucent; refractive index about 1.53 to 1.54. Slightly porous, which allows dyeing, which is stable. Hard and tough, it has been cut into cabochons, signets, beads, intaglios and above all cameos since antiquity.",
